        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(terminal-core): prevent String.replace $ pattern injection in display-string",
        "body": "fix(terminal-core): prevent String.replace $ pattern injection in display-string\n\n## Description\n\n`String.prototype.replace()` with a string second argument interprets `$` sequences as special replacement patterns (`$&`, `` $` ``, `$'`, `$1`-`$9`, `$<name>`). When the user's home directory path contains such characters (e.g. `/home/$&data`), the replacement produces a corrupted display path.\n\n## Fix\n\nUsing a replacer function `() => fallbackHome` instead of the raw string argument prevents `$` pattern interpretation, ensuring the literal home directory path is used regardless of its content.\n\n## Test evidence (vitest, 3/3 passed)\n\n```\nTest Files  1 passed (1)\n     Tests  3 passed (3)\n```\n\n```\n ✓ displayString > shortens whole-value homes and child paths without clipping sibling prefixes\n ✓ displayString > uses OPENCLAW_HOME as the display prefix\n ✓ displayString > preserves literal $& in home path replacement target\n```\n\n## Real terminal evidence\n\n```\n=== fix(terminal-core): prevent String.replace $ pattern injection ===\nCommit: a6fb22b7c74\nDate:   2026-07-19T16:11:36Z\n\n=== Test suite (vitest, 3/3 passed) ===\n[test] starting test/vitest/vitest.unit.config.ts\n\n RUN  v4.1.10 /home/lizeyu/workspace/openclaw\n\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  3 passed (3)\n   Start at  00:11:44\n   Duration  426ms (transform 206ms, setup 222ms, import 4ms, tests 60ms, environment 0ms)\n\n[test] passed 1 Vitest shard in 7.57s\n```\n\nThe new regression test explicitly covers the scenario where the resolved OS home directory path contains `$&` (a `String.prototype.replace()` special pattern), verifying that the replacer function prevents pattern interpretation.\n\n## Diff\n\n```diff\n--- a/packages/terminal-core/src/display-string.ts\n+++ b/packages/terminal-core/src/display-string.ts\n@@ -49,7 +49,7 @@ function resolveRawHomeDir(\n   const explicitHome = normalize(env.OPENCLAW_HOME);\n   if (explicitHome) {\n     const fallbackHome = resolveRawOsHomeDir(env, homedir);\n-    return fallbackHome ? explicitHome.replace(/^~(?=$|[\\/])/, fallbackHome) : explicitHome;\n+    return fallbackHome ? explicitHome.replace(/^~(?=$|[\\/])/, () => fallbackHome) : explicitHome;\n   }\n   return resolveRawOsHomeDir(env, homedir);\n }\n```",
        "branch": "fix/replace-home-dollar-injection",
